menu "espOS WiFi"

    config ESPOS_WIFI_MAX_NETWORKS
        int "Configured networks (priority slots)"
        default 4
        range 1 4
        help
            Number of ssidN/pskN/bssidN slots honoured from the "wifi"
            namespace (the descriptor declares four).

            The mDNS responder that used to be configured here moved to
            espos_net with the seam: CONFIG_ESPOS_NET_MDNS and
            CONFIG_ESPOS_NET_MDNS_MAX_SERVICES under "espOS network".

    config ESPOS_WIFI_DRAIN_TASK_STACK
        int "Driver action task stack size (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 3072 16384
        help
            The task that runs the state machine's driver calls (connect,
            disconnect, the portal), reports the link to espos_net with its
            subscriber callbacks, and publishes the status to the web UI.
            These ran on the event, timer or HTTP task that dispatched them
            until they moved here, so the event loop no longer waits on a
            radio that is slow to answer.

    config ESPOS_WIFI_DRAIN_TASK_PRIO
        int "Driver action task priority"
        default 19
        range 1 24
        help
            FreeRTOS priority of the driver action task. Just below the
            default event loop (20), which ran this work before: a connect
            or the report that brings the network up does not wait behind
            application tasks, and the event loop still delivers the radio's
            answers first.

endmenu
